@startuml grammar-corrector-colocation
' Co-location: the importer's store router and the query's view router are the SAME
' pure function of (first_token, order). So the shard that STORES a key answers it.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/grammar-corrector-colocation.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 2 in docs/integration/multi-shard-grammar-corrector.md
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title Co-location — the store route equals the query route

legend top right
  |= Color |= Path |
  |<#00838F>     | Import (write) |
  |<#1565C0>     | Query (read) |
  |<#6A1B9A>     | Shared pure router |
endlegend

rectangle "**Importer**\nn-gram tokens [w₀, w₁, …]" as imp #00838F
rectangle "**route_tokens(tokens)**\nfirst = tokens[0], order = |tokens|" as rt #00838F
rectangle "**ShardedView::view_for(first_id, key_len)**\nfirst = get_term(first_id), order = key_len" as vf #1565C0

rectangle "**compute_shard_key_from_token(first, order, granularity)**\nhash(first)  —or—  prefix(first, order)" as csk #6A1B9A
rectangle "**ShardKey**" as sk #6A1B9A

rectangle "**store_in_shard(key, varint(ids), count)**\nget_or_create — write path" as store #00838F
rectangle "**get_shard_readonly(key)**\nresident-or-open-only — read path" as read #1565C0
rectangle "**One physical shard trie**" as shard #455A64

imp --> rt
rt --> csk : (first, order)
vf --> csk : (first, order)
csk --> sk
sk --> store
sk --> read
store --> shard : writes
read --> shard : reads

note bottom of shard #E3F2FD
  Both sides call the identical pure function on the identical (first_token, order),
  so every exact key is answered by the shard that stored it. Under Adaptive
  granularity the router must use the PRODUCED length key_len (|h|+1 for the
  successor oracle), not the history length — else order-1 vs order-≥2 split apart.
end note
@enduml
